From 396e26a020569f48ed36f06b87fa0a1bb00237bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VERHILLE Arnaud <gist974@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:10:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] 68020 core: the discarded refill is an instruction
 fetch without a cache too

readStatusRefill() sent the discarded program word through readInstr() only
when the instruction cache is emulated. Without one, it used a plain program
read, which skips what readInstr() charges every other instruction word
fetched from a port narrower than 32 bits (dsack()).

The refill now goes through readInstr() on every 68020-core model, so the
discarded word costs what any other fetched word costs on that bus. The
manuals count it as an ordinary prefetch bus cycle: an instruction prefetch
is one bus cycle on a 32-bit port and two on a 16-bit port (MC68020UM
Table 5-6, MC68030UM Table 7-6), and the timing tables charge the refill
word the instruction discards like any other prefetch: MOVE EA,SR is
11(0/2/0) worst case against 5(0/1/0) for MOVE EA,CCR, an expired DBcc
10(0/3/0), a taken TRAPV 32(1/2/5) (MC68020UM 8.2, 8.2.7, 8.2.15, 8.2.17;
MC68030UM 11.2.2, 11.3.3, 11.6.7, 11.6.15, 11.6.17, 12.7.1).

The change matters only where the instruction cache is not emulated, the
68040 models: the 68020 and 68030 already went through readInstr(). There
the charge follows the host's dsack() answer, and with the default 16-bit
answer a 68040 pays it although MC68040UM 7.2 says the 68040 does not
size its bus dynamically: a host that models a 68040 bus answers
DSACK_32.
---
 Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
index dd92749..2cf66f1 100644
--- a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
+++ b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
@@ -870,10 +870,8 @@ Moira::readStatusRefill()
 {
     u32 addr = C == Core::C68000 ? reg.pc : reg.pc + 2;
     if constexpr (C == Core::C68020) {
-        if (iCache.emulated) {
-            (void)readInstr<C>(addr);
-            return;
-        }
+        (void)readInstr<C>(addr);
+        return;
     }
     (void)read<C, AddrSpace::PROG, Word>(addr);
 }
